1. Understanding Maven Project Structure
\f1\b0\fs24 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa100\partightenfactor0

\f2 \cf0 Maven standardizes the project structure for both Java and web-based applications. src/
\f1 \

\f2 \uc0\u9500 \u9472 \u9472  main/
\f1 \

\f2 \uc0\u9474  \'a0 \'a0\u9500 \u9472 \u9472  java/ \'a0 \'a0 \'a0 \'a0\u8594  Application source code
\f1 \

\f2 \uc0\u9474  \'a0 \'a0\u9492 \u9472 \u9472  resources/ \'a0 \u8594  Configuration files like config.properties
\f1 \

\f2 \uc0\u9492 \u9472 \u9472  test/
\f1 \

\f2 \'a0 \'a0 \'a0\uc0\u9500 \u9472 \u9472  java/ \'a0 \'a0 \'a0 \'a0\u8594  Unit test source code
\f1 \

\f2 \'a0 \'a0 \'a0\uc0\u9492 \u9472 \u9472  resources/ \'a0 \u8594  Test resources
\f1 \

\f2 The compiled files and reports are generated in the 
\f3\b\fs20 target/
\f2\b0\fs24  directory after a successful build.
\f1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

